  "verdict": "The unique double-sealed M2050 attempt and result support a narrow multi-layer, multi-token component-cycle distribution claim. The fixed performance-independent selection contains 192 workloads from four sealed ep34 sequences, all 12 FC1 layers supported by the G48 frontend, four G48-supported FC2 layers, and first/middle/last B4 token quartets. Independent full re-decoding of every selected descriptor from the sealed M1707 fc_frames payload reproduced fixture, metadata and packed statistics byte-for-byte. All 192 VCS logs contain one unique PASS, no fatal/assertion/timeout signature, and nonzero signed-bridge, stale-attack and reset-recovery covers. An independent age/tie-aware LRU4 model reproduced all metadata and RTL-checked counters. Totals are 1,381,704 ordinary-LRU4 cycles versus 551,343 TSBG cycles, or 2.506070x and 60.0969% less component execution time; scalar weight-bank requests fall from 968,064 to 335,328, or 65.3610%. The 19 empty workloads remain in every aggregate. The result is not full-FC, all-FC2, real-weight, same-area, macro-inclusive, power, energy or system evidence.",
